---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

const software = await getCollection("software");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research methodology"
  description="How church software entries are selected, sourced, dated, corrected and separated from editorial assessment and commercial interests."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Methodology" }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container page-grid">
      <article class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Trust and evidence</p>
        <h1>Research methodology</h1>
        <p>
          The directory publishes facts that can be traced to a dated source.
          A current official supplier page is sufficient evidence for what the
          supplier publishes; it does not amount to hands-on testing or
          independent certification.
        </p>

        <h2>Which products are included</h2>
        <p>
          A product must have an active official site and plausible relevance to
          UK church administration, ministry or operations. The directory currently
          contains {software.length} entries and is not a market-wide shortlist.
        </p>

        <h2>How facts are researched</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Prefer official product, pricing, support and policy pages.</li>
          <li>Record the source URL, checked date and fields it supports.</li>
          <li>Keep structured facts separate from directory assessment.</li>
          <li>Omit incidental details that do not have useful supporting evidence.</li>
          <li>Turn material gaps into a precise question for the supplier.</li>
          <li>Do not infer compliance from general marketing language.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>How sources are described</h2>
        <dl class="stack">
          <div>
            <dt>Supplier source</dt>
            <dd>
              A current official product, pricing, support, policy or terms page
              supports what the supplier publishes.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Independent source</dt>
            <dd>
              A relevant public record, regulator, authoritative body or other
              non-supplier source supports the fact.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Directory tested</dt>
            <dd>
              Church Software UK performed and documented the stated test. This
              label is not used unless that work actually occurred.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>

        <h2>When a detail is missing</h2>
        <p>
          Optional details are omitted. Matters that could change a purchasing
          decision—such as hosting, Gift Aid, contracts or data export—become
          specific questions to settle. “No” is used only when a suitable source
          explicitly establishes absence.
        </p>

        <h2>Review cycle</h2>
        <p>
          The automated stale check currently flags entries more than 180 days
          after their last checked date. A recent date does not mean every product
          detail is complete.
        </p>

        <h2>Corrections</h2>
        <p>
          Corrections will be assessed on evidence, regardless of commercial status.
          No public correction route is currently configured, so the directory is
          not ready for public launch until a responsible publisher and contact
          route are confirmed.
        </p>

        <h2>Commercial independence</h2>
        <p>
          Affiliate links are used only where a relationship is confirmed and
          disclosed beside the relevant link. They must not guarantee positive
          coverage or ranking. Any sponsored listing must be clearly labelled
          and is held to the same research and editorial standards.
        </p>
        <h2>How AI is used</h2>
        <p>
          AI may help organise research, identify missing fields and draft copy.
          It is not treated as a source of product facts. A human remains
          responsible for checking evidence and approving published material.
        </p>
      </article>
      <aside class="aside-card">
        <h2>Important boundary</h2>
        <p>
          Churches should check legal, security, safeguarding, tax, data-hosting
          and contractual matters directly with suppliers and appropriate
          advisers.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/update-a-listing/">Point to a correction</a></p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
